1968 ( [LINK: (MCMLXVIII) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_numerals] ) was a  [LINK: (leap year starting on Monday) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leap_year_starting_on_Monday]  of the  [LINK: (Gregorian calendar) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gregorian_calendar] , the 1968th year of the  [LINK: (Common Era) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_Era]  (CE) and  [LINK: (Anno Domini) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anno_Domini]  (AD) designations, the 968th  year of the  [LINK: (2nd millennium) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2nd_millennium] , the 68th  year of the  [LINK: (20th century) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/20th_century] , and the  9th   year of the  [LINK: (1960s) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1960s]  decade.


# EVENTS #

[LINK: (January) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_1968]  – The  [LINK: (I'm Backing Britain campaign) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I%27m_Backing_Britain]  starts spontaneously.

[LINK: (January 5) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_5]  –  [LINK: (Prague Spring) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prague_Spring] :  [LINK: (Alexander Dubček) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_Dub%C4%8Dek]  is chosen as leader of the  [LINK: (Communist Party of Czechoslovakia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Communist_Party_of_Czechoslovakia] . [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1968#cite_note-1]

[LINK: (January 10) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_10]  –  [LINK: (John Gorton) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Gorton]  is sworn in as 19th  [LINK: (Prime Minister of Australia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prime_Minister_of_Australia] , taking over from  [LINK: (John McEwen) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_McEwen]  after being  [LINK: (elected leader) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1968_Liberal_Party_of_Australia_leadership_election]  of the  [LINK: (Liberal Party) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liberal_Party_of_Australia]  the previous day, following the  [LINK: (disappearance of Harold Holt) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Disappearance_of_Harold_Holt] . Gorton becomes the only  [LINK: (Senator) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_Senate]  to become Prime Minister, though he immediately transfers to the  [LINK: (House of Representatives) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_House_of_Representatives]  through the  [LINK: (1968 Higgins by-election) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1968_Higgins_by-election]  in Holt's vacant seat.

[LINK: (January 15) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_15]  – The  [LINK: (1968 Belice earthquake) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1968_Belice_earthquake]  in  [LINK: (Sicily) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sicily]  kills 380 and injures around 1,000. [LINK: ([2]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1968#cite_note-2]  [LINK: ([3]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1968#cite_note-3]

[LINK: (January 21) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_21] 
 [LINK: (Vietnam War) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vietnam_War] :  [LINK: (Battle of Khe Sanh) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Khe_Sanh]  – One of the most publicized and controversial battles of the war begins, ending on  [LINK: (April 8) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/April_8] .
 [LINK: (1968 Thule Air Base B-52 crash) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1968_Thule_Air_Base_B-52_crash] : A U.S.  [LINK: (B-52 Stratofortress) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/B-52_Stratofortress]  crashes in Greenland, discharging 4  [LINK: (nuclear bombs) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuclear_bomb] . [LINK: ([4]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1968#cite_note-4]

[LINK: (Vietnam War) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vietnam_War] :  [LINK: (Battle of Khe Sanh) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Khe_Sanh]  – One of the most publicized and controversial battles of the war begins, ending on  [LINK: (April 8) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/April_8] .

[LINK: (1968 Thule Air Base B-52 crash) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1968_Thule_Air_Base_B-52_crash] : A U.S.  [LINK: (B-52 Stratofortress) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/B-52_Stratofortress]  crashes in Greenland, discharging 4  [LINK: (nuclear bombs) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuclear_bomb] . [LINK: ([4]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1968#cite_note-4]

[LINK: (January 23) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_23]  –  [LINK: (North Korea) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Korea]  seizes the  [LINK: (USS Pueblo) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/USS_Pueblo_(AGER-2)] , claiming the ship violated its territorial waters while spying.

[LINK: (January 25) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_25]  –  [LINK: (Israeli) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Israel]  submarine  [LINK: (INS Dakar) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/INS_Dakar]  sinks in the Mediterranean Sea, killing 69. [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1968#cite_note-5]

[LINK: (January 28) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_28]  –  [LINK: (French) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/France]  submarine  [LINK: (Minerve) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_submarine_Minerve_(S647)]  sinks in the Mediterranean Sea, killing 52.

[LINK: (January 30) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_30]  –  [LINK: (Vietnam War) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vietnam_War] : The  [LINK: (Tet Offensive) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tet_Offensive]  begins as  [LINK: (Viet Cong) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viet_Cong]  forces launch a series of surprise attacks across  [LINK: (South Vietnam) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Vietnam] .

[LINK: (January 31) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_31] 
 [LINK: (Viet Cong) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viet_Cong]  soldiers attack the  [LINK: (Embassy of the United States, Saigon) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Embassy_of_the_United_States,_Saigon] .
 [LINK: (Nauru) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nauru]  president  [LINK: (Hammer DeRoburt) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hammer_DeRoburt]  declares independence from  [LINK: (Australia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australia] , Britain and New Zealand. [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1968#cite_note-6]

[LINK: (Viet Cong) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viet_Cong]  soldiers attack the  [LINK: (Embassy of the United States, Saigon) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Embassy_of_the_United_States,_Saigon] .

[LINK: (Nauru) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nauru]  president  [LINK: (Hammer DeRoburt) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hammer_DeRoburt]  declares independence from  [LINK: (Australia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australia] , Britain and New Zealand. [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1968#cite_note-6]

[LINK: (February 1) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1] 
 [LINK: (Vietnam War) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vietnam_War] :  [LINK: (Execution of Nguyễn Văn Lém) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Execution_of_Nguy%E1%BB%85n_V%C4%83n_L%C3%A9m]  – A  [LINK: (Viet Cong) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viet_Cong]  officer is  [LINK: (summarily executed) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Summary_execution]  by  [LINK: (Nguyễn Ngọc Loan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nguy%E1%BB%85n_Ng%E1%BB%8Dc_Loan] , a  [LINK: (South Vietnamese) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Vietnam]  National Police Chief. The event is photographed by  [LINK: (Eddie Adams) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eddie_Adams_(photographer)] . The photo makes headlines around the world, eventually winning the  [LINK: (1969 Pulitzer Prize) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1969_Pulitzer_Prize] , and sways U.S. public opinion against the war.
The  [LINK: (Pennsylvania Railroad) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pennsylvania_Railroad]  and the  [LINK: (New York Central Railroad) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_Central_Railroad]  merge to form  [LINK: (Penn Central) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Penn_Central] , the largest ever corporate  [LINK: (merger) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mergers_and_acquisitions]  up to this date.

[LINK: (Vietnam War) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vietnam_War] :  [LINK: (Execution of Nguyễn Văn Lém) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Execution_of_Nguy%E1%BB%85n_V%C4%83n_L%C3%A9m]  – A  [LINK: (Viet Cong) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viet_Cong]  officer is  [LINK: (summarily executed) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Summary_execution]  by  [LINK: (Nguyễn Ngọc Loan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nguy%E1%BB%85n_Ng%E1%BB%8Dc_Loan] , a  [LINK: (South Vietnamese) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Vietnam]  National Police Chief. The event is photographed by  [LINK: (Eddie Adams) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eddie_Adams_(photographer)] . The photo makes headlines around the world, eventually winning the  [LINK: (1969 Pulitzer Prize) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1969_Pulitzer_Prize] , and sways U.S. public opinion against the war.

The  [LINK: (Pennsylvania Railroad) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pennsylvania_Railroad]  and the  [LINK: (New York Central Railroad) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_Central_Railroad]  merge to form  [LINK: (Penn Central) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Penn_Central] , the largest ever corporate  [LINK: (merger) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mergers_and_acquisitions]  up to this date.

[LINK: (February 6) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_6] – [LINK: (18) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_18]  – The  [LINK: (1968 Winter Olympics) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1968_Winter_Olympics]  are held in  [LINK: (Grenoble) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grenoble] , France.

[LINK: (February 8) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_8]  –  [LINK: (Civil rights movement) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Civil_rights_movement]  in the United States:  [LINK: (Orangeburg Massacre) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orangeburg_Massacre]  – A civil rights demonstration on a college campus to protest  [LINK: (de facto) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/De_facto]   [LINK: (racial segregation) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Racial_segregation_in_the_United_States]  in  [LINK: (South Carolina) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Carolina]  is broken up by highway patrolmen; three African American students are killed, the first instance of police killing student protestors at an American campus.

[LINK: (February 12) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_12]  –  [LINK: (Vietnam War) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vietnam_War] :  [LINK: (Phong Nhị and Phong Nhất massacre) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phong_Nh%E1%BB%8B_and_Phong_Nh%E1%BA%A5t_massacre] .

[LINK: (February 19) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_19]  – The television series  [LINK: (Mister Rogers' Neighborhood) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mister_Rogers%27_Neighborhood]  premieres on  [LINK: (National Educational Television) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Educational_Television]  in the United States and becomes one of the longest running children's shows ever.

[LINK: (February 24) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_24]  –  [LINK: (Vietnam War) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vietnam_War] : The  [LINK: (Tet Offensive) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tet_Offensive]  is halted;  [LINK: (South Vietnam) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Vietnam]  recaptures  [LINK: (Huế) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hu%E1%BA%BF] .

[LINK: (February 25) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_25]  –  [LINK: (Vietnam War) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vietnam_War] :  [LINK: (Hà My massacre) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/H%C3%A0_My_massacre] .

[LINK: (March 1) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/March_1] 
 [LINK: (Commonwealth Immigrants Act 1968) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Commonwealth_Immigrants_Act_1968]  further reduces right of entry for citizens from the  [LINK: (British Commonwealth) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/British_Commonwealth]  to the United Kingdom.
First performance of an  [LINK: (Andrew Lloyd Webber) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andrew_Lloyd_Webber] – [LINK: (Tim Rice) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tim_Rice]  musical,  [LINK: (Joseph and the Amazing Technicolor Dreamcoat) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joseph_and_the_Amazing_Technicolor_Dreamcoat]  in its original form as a "pop  [LINK: (cantata) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cantata] ", by pupils of a private school in London. [LINK: ([7]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1968#cite_note-7]  [LINK: ([8]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1968#cite_note-8]  [LINK: ([9]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1968#cite_note-9]

[LINK: (Commonwealth Immigrants Act 1968) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Commonwealth_Immigrants_Act_1968]  further reduces right of entry for citizens from the  [LINK: (British Commonwealth) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/British_Commonwealth]  to the United Kingdom.

First performance of an  [LINK: (Andrew Lloyd Webber) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andrew_Lloyd_Webber] – [LINK: (Tim Rice) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tim_Rice]  musical,  [LINK: (Joseph and the Amazing Technicolor Dreamcoat) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joseph_and_the_Amazing_Technicolor_Dreamcoat]  in its original form as a "pop  [LINK: (cantata) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cantata] ", by pupils of a private school in London. [LINK: ([7]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1968#cite_note-7]  [LINK: ([8]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1968#cite_note-8]  [LINK: ([9]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1968#cite_note-9]

[LINK: (March 2) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/March_2]  –  [LINK: (Baggeridge Colliery) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baggeridge_Colliery]  closes marking the end of over 300 years of  [LINK: (coal mining) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coal_mining]  in the  [LINK: (Black Country) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Country]  of England. [LINK: ([10]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1968#cite_note-10]

[LINK: (March 3) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/March_3]  –  [LINK: (Air France Flight 212) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Air_France_Flight_212_(1968)] , a  [LINK: (Boeing 707) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boeing_707] , crashes in  [LINK: (Guadeloupe) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guadeloupe]  while approaching an airport. As a result, 63 people die.

