[LINK: (December 10) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/December_10]  – Japan's biggest heist, the never-solved " [LINK: (300 million yen robbery) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/300_million_yen_robbery] ", occurs in Tokyo.

[LINK: (December 11) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/December_11]  – The film  [LINK: (Oliver!) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oliver!_(film)]  based on the hit London and  [LINK: (Broadway) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Broadway_theatre]  musical, opens in the U.S. after being released first in the UK. It goes on to win the  [LINK: (Academy Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Academy_Award]  for  [LINK: (Best Picture) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture] .

[LINK: (December 13) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/December_13]  – Prompted by growing unrest and a perceived proliferation of "pro-communist" violent actions,  [LINK: (Brazilian) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brazil]   [LINK: (president) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_Brazil]   [LINK: (Artur da Costa e Silva) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artur_da_Costa_e_Silva]  enacts the so-called  [LINK: (AI-5) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI-5] , the fifth of a series of non-constitutional emergency decrees allegedly to help "stabilize" the country after the turmoils of the early 1960s.

[LINK: (December 20) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/December_20]  – The first known  [LINK: (Zodiac Killer) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zodiac_Killer]  murder takes place in Lake Herman Road,  [LINK: (Vallejo) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vallejo,_California] ,  [LINK: (California) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/California] .

[LINK: (December 22) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/December_22]  –  [LINK: (Mao Zedong) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mao_Zedong]  advocates that educated urban youth in China be sent for re-education in the  [LINK: (countryside) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rural_area] . It marks the start of the  [LINK: ("Up to the mountains and down to the villages" movement) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Down_to_the_Countryside_Movement] .

[LINK: (December 24) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/December_24]  –  [LINK: (Apollo program) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_program] : The crewed U.S. spacecraft  [LINK: (Apollo 8) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_8]  enters orbit around the  [LINK: (Moon) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moon] . Astronauts  [LINK: (Frank Borman) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frank_Borman] ,  [LINK: (Jim Lovell) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jim_Lovell]  and  [LINK: (William Anders) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Anders]  become the first humans to see the  [LINK: (far side) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Far_side_(Moon)]  of the  [LINK: (Moon) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moon]  and planet  [LINK: (Earth) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earth]  as a whole, as well as having traveled further away from Earth than any people in history. Anders photographs  [LINK: (Earthrise) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earthrise] . The crew also give a  [LINK: (reading from the Book of Genesis) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_8_Genesis_reading] .

[LINK: (December 28) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/December_28]  –  [LINK: (1968 Israeli raid on Lebanon) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1968_Israeli_raid_on_Lebanon] : Israeli forces fly into  [LINK: (Lebanese) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lebanon]  airspace, launching an attack on the airport in  [LINK: (Beirut) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beirut]  and destroying more than a dozen aircraft.

The  [LINK: (Khmer Rouge) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khmer_Rouge]  is officially formed in  [LINK: (Cambodia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cambodia]  as an offshoot movement of the  [LINK: (Vietnam People's Army) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vietnam_People%27s_Army]  from  [LINK: (North Vietnam) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Vietnam]  to bring communism to the nation. A few years later, they will become bitter enemies.

Drainage of the  [LINK: (Flevopolder) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flevopolder]  in the Netherlands is completed, creating by some definitions the largest  [LINK: (artificial island) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_island]  in the world. [LINK: ([36]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1968#cite_note-36]  [LINK: ([37]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1968#cite_note-37]

An oil field is confirmed in Northern Alaska: the  [LINK: (Prudhoe Bay Oil Field) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prudhoe_Bay_Oil_Field] .


